-rwxr-xr-x 1 runner runner 14862410 Oct  8 23:30 wormhole-william
Create a (magic) Wormhole and communicate through it.

  Wormholes are created by speaking the same magic CODE in two different
  places at the same time. Wormholes are secure against anyone who doesn't
  use the same code.

Usage:
  wormhole-william [command]

Available Commands:
  completion       Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  help             Help about any command
  receive          Receive a text message, file, or directory...
  send             Send a text message, file, or directory...
  shell-completion Generate shell completion script

Flags:
  -h, --help               help for wormhole-william
      --relay-url string   rendezvous relay to use
  -v, --version            version for wormhole-william

Use "wormhole-william [command] --help" for more information about a command.
---- SEND HELP
Send a text message, file, or directory...

Usage:
  wormhole-william send [WHAT] [flags]

Flags:
      --code string       human-generated code phrase
  -c, --code-length int   length of code (in bytes/words)
  -h, --help              help for send
      --hide-progress     suppress progress-bar display
      --qr                display code as QR code (experimental)
      --text string       text message to send, instead of a file.
                          Use '-' to read from stdin
  -v, --verify            display verification string (and wait for approval)

Global Flags:
      --relay-url string   rendezvous relay to use
---- RECV HELP
Receive a text message, file, or directory...

Usage:
  wormhole-william receive [OPTIONS] [CODE]... [flags]

Aliases:
  receive, recv

Flags:
  -h, --help            help for receive
      --hide-progress   suppress progress-bar display
  -v, --verify          display verification string (and wait for approval)

Global Flags:
      --relay-url string   rendezvous relay to use
